menu "Example Configuration"
    config EXAMPLE_SLEEP_TIME_MS
        int "Light sleep time (ms)"
        default 1000
        range 1 86400000
        help
            How long to stay in light sleep after one frame is captured.
            The unit is milliseconds. The timer starts when esp_light_sleep_start()
            is called. The full software AOV cycle is this interval plus one capture.

    config EXAMPLE_CT_MIN
        int "Minimum color temperature (K)"
        default 3000
        range 2000 20000
        help
            After init, keep streaming until the IPA color temperature is at least this value.
            Later captures reuse the registers kept across light sleep.

    config EXAMPLE_CT_MAX
        int "Maximum color temperature (K)"
        default 8000
        range EXAMPLE_CT_MIN 20000
        help
            After init, keep streaming until the IPA color temperature is at most this value.

    config EXAMPLE_CT_WAIT_MS
        int "Color temperature wait timeout (ms)"
        default 30000
        range 1000 300000
        help
            Stop this boot if color temperature is still outside the range after this time.
            The device does not capture a frame and does not enter light sleep.

    config EXAMPLE_RECV_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Frame receive timeout (ms)"
        default 1000
        range 10 60000
        help
            DQBUF timeout. While waiting for color temperature, each DQBUF uses
            the smaller of this value and the remaining wait deadline.
endmenu
